---
title: Opening Acclamation (Holy Baptism)
type: acclamation
citation: BCP 299
bulletin: full
---

[Rubric] *The people standing, the Celebrant says*
[Celebrant] Blessed be God: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.
[People] **And blessed be his kingdom, now and for ever. Amen.**
[Rubric] *In place of the above, from Easter Day through the Day of Pentecost*
[Celebrant] Alleluia. Christ is risen.
[People] **The Lord is risen indeed. Alleluia.**
[Rubric] *In Lent and on other penitential occasions*
[Celebrant] Bless the Lord who forgives all our sins;
[People] **His mercy endures forever.**
[Rubric] *The Celebrant then continues*
[Celebrant] There is one Body and one Spirit;
[People] **There is one hope in God's call to us;**

---

[Celebrant] One Lord, one Faith, one Baptism;
[People] **One God and Father of all.**
[Celebrant] The Lord be with you.
[People] **And also with you.**
[Celebrant] Let us pray.
